To convert a text string to upper case, you can use the `upper()` function in most programming languages. Here's how you can do it in a few popular languages:

**Python:**
```python
text = "Hello, World!"
upper_text = text.upper()
print(upper_text) # Output: HELLO, WORLD!
```

**Java:**
```java
String text = "Hello, World!";
String upperText = text.toUpperCase();
out.println(upperText); // Output: HELLO, WORLD!
```

**JavaScript:**
```javascript
let text = "Hello, World!";
let upperText = text.toUpperCase();
console.log(upper_text); // Output: HELLO, WORLD!
```

**C++:**
```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <string>

int main() {
 std::string text = "Hello, World!";
 std::string upperText = text;
 for (char &c : upperText) {
 c = std::toupper(c);
 }
 std::cout << upperText << std::endl; // Output: HELLO, WORLD!
 return 0;
}
```

